# No noise / placeholder Desktop icons (hard rule)

Operator defect (2026-08): Desktop **Jump Config** showed a
**multi-colored noise/static** icon (plus the UAC shield). That pattern
is a known suite failure mode — not a Windows quirk to ignore.

## The rule

> **Never ship Desktop, Start Menu, or Add/Remove Programs icons that
> render as random-bit / noise / static pixels. Every advertised
> shortcut and every shipping PE icon resource must use a
> PNG-compressed AIC `.ico` from `core-assets` (or a validated
> installer-shortcuts derivative). Empty shortcut `IconLocation`,
> EXE resource index 0 when that EXE embeds a noise ICO, BMP/DIB-only
> ICO frames, and `aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png` (or any
> same-family noise bitmap) are forbidden on operator-facing chrome.**

## Why shortcuts become noise (RCA contract)

Any one of these produces the static tile operators report:

| Cause | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| **Shortcut `IconLocation` empty / `,0`** | Explorer extracts the target EXE’s icon resource. If that PE embeds a bad Tauri `icon.ico`, the Desktop tile is noise (+ UAC shield when elevated). |
| **Stale `src-tauri/icons/icon.ico`** | Historical `tauri icon` / unsynced tree left a 207 KB noise ICO in Jump / DB Mgmt / WA / Recording / sibling Tauri apps. `core-assets/icons/tauri` empty → `sync-to-projects.ps1` tree-sync is a no-op and leaves the noise in place. |
| **BMP/DIB-only `.ico` (ImageMagick 7.1 default)** | Windows Explorer paints BMP frames as multi-colored static. Canonical generators assemble **PNG-compressed** ICO only (`generate-icons.ps1`, `generate-installer-shortcut-icons.ps1`). |
| **Missing staged `aic-icon.ico`** | Side-load / incomplete MSI under `%ProgramFiles%\AIC\…` has the Tauri EXE but no sidecar `aic-icon.ico`; sync scripts that omit `IconLocation` fall back to the EXE. |
| **Header / in-app placeholder** | `core-assets/branding/aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png` (64×64 colored noise) must never re-enter `src/assets/` or be used as an icon source. See `pim-offline-client/AGENTS.md` brand-image rule and [`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc). |

## Required patterns

1. **Canonical mark** — `core-assets/icons/desktop/aic-icon.ico` (or
   `icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/*.ico` for MSI product / per-shortcut
   variants). Produce derivatives only inside `core-assets`, then sync
   ([`branding-assets.mdc`](branding-assets.mdc)).
2. **PNG-compressed ICO** — at least one PNG payload per file. Refuse
   BMP/DIB-only at stage time (`Stage-InstallerShortcutIcons.ps1`,
   Jump/DB/Recording/WA MSI builders).
3. **Shortcut `IconLocation`** — every Desktop / Start Menu `.lnk` for a
   configurator MUST set
   `IconLocation = "<installDir>\aic-icon.ico,0"` (or the WiX-advertised
   `Icon=` resource). Never rely on bare EXE `,0` for suite products.
4. **Tauri PE resources** — `src-tauri/icons/` comes from
   `core-assets/icons/tauri` via `sync-to-projects.ps1`. If that tree is
   empty, regenerate with
   `cargo tauri icon icons/source/aic-icon-1024.png --output icons/tauri`
   **in core-assets**, commit, sync — do not invent local noise ICOs.
5. **Section 508 / credibility** — brand image must be the real AIC mark,
   not the noise placeholder ([`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc)
   §2 pointer; [`operator-ui-credibility.mdc`](operator-ui-credibility.mdc)).

## Forbidden constructs

- `New-Object WScript.Shell` / WiX `<Shortcut>` without an explicit AIC
  icon path or `Icon="ProductIcon"` backed by staged `aic-icon.ico`.
- Committing or syncing `aic-header.PLACEHOLDER-do-not-use.png` (or any
  random-bit bitmap) as `icon.ico`, `aic-icon.ico`, or header art.
- `magick … out.ico` without the PNG-compressed assembly path documented
  in `core-assets/icons/desktop/installer-shortcuts/README.md`.
- Claiming a Desktop icon fix without a screenshot of the live shortcut
  tile (or an extracted PNG from the shortcut’s `IconLocation` target).

## Jump Config worked example (2026-08)

**Broken:** `Jump Config.lnk` →
`…\pim-jump-server-configurator-tauri.exe` with `IconLocation = ,0`;
install dir missing `aic-icon.ico`; EXE embeds noise `icon.ico`.

**Fixed:** stage `core-assets/icons/desktop/aic-icon.ico` as
`%ProgramFiles%\AIC\PimJumpServer\aic-icon.ico` (or MSI `JumpServer`);
set shortcut `IconLocation` to that file; keep Tauri `src-tauri/icons`
synced from `core-assets/icons/tauri`.

